  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a woman in a hijab with two contrasting text overlays. The top text asks, \"how can this be allowed a free home and benefits?\" while the bottom text states, \"when this man was allowed to die on the streets after serving this country.\" The juxtaposition implies a comparison between a woman receiving social benefits and a man who died on the streets, suggesting the woman is undeserving or greedy. This framing is hateful as it targets individuals based on gender and religious identity (hijab), implying that women who receive government assistance are morally or ethically inferior to men who died in service. The meme uses the woman's appearance to reinforce a negative stereotype, suggesting she is undeserving of aid, while simultaneously implying that men who died in service are more deserving. This is a direct attack on individuals based on gender and religious identity, fitting the definition of hateful content.",
